From f5663b5edc68bee7ef528628c5b1cd39b8d10dfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hyunW3 <0176778602@naver.com>
Date: Mon, 8 Jun 2026 16:08:11 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] aunet: before_root:bt online generation (port of
 spacebyte _generate_online_bt)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes degenerate BPEByte free generation. The stock get_levels_mask_gen marks
EVERY generated byte as a patch boundary (the last char of any prefix is always
a BPE token-end), so sampling diverges hard from the offline before-root
boundaries used in training/likelihood. Reproduces the spacebyte_feasibility
generate-branch approach: full-recompute forward (use_cache=False) + per-row
incremental parser + speculative-sample-then-rollback.

- regex_cutting.py: BPEIncrementalBTParser gains the online interface
  feed / committed_levels / snapshot / restore / pos_at_root, plus a
  commit_margin. llama3 is merge-rank (not longest-match) BPE, so a single new
  byte can re-segment a prefix and move a boundary back across the previous
  token-end (" qu"|"ic" -> " quick"); margin=2 holds the last two token-ends
  speculative so generation never commits a boundary it must retract. finalize()
  ignores the margin and still equals the offline get_levels_mask (verified).
- hierarchical.py: forward_logits(tokens, level_mask) — non-cached logits-only
  forward (same encoder/trunk/decoder path as training forward, no targets).
- generate_bt.py: online_bt_loop (forward_fn-injectable, CPU-testable) +
  generate_online_bt (real-model entry via forward_logits). Resyncs the mask
  from the parser's committed view each step and rolls back to the earliest
  pre-sample boundary change; per-position backstop guards residual oscillation.
- test_generate_bt.py: parser feed/finalize==offline (50 random), snapshot/
  restore round-trip, committed subset of offline, and forced-target generation
  reconstructing offline boundaries (single + batch). All pass on CPU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
